ed method, model, estimator, metric, or data\nsource with a different one. A search result is only a compact candidate: when\nit appears relevant, inspect that tool before rejecting the ordinary-tool\nroute. Use a UDT only when no plausible candidate exists or targeted inspection\nshows that the required operation is unavailable.\n\n### Galaxy Access\n\nUse `search_galaxy_tools` with concise tool-family, operation, package, or\ntarget-metric terms for live ordinary-tool discovery; do not recreate tool\nsearch with BioBlend `get_tools()`. Use the available Galaxy MCP execution tools\nfor supported inspection, submission, and blocking execution. In\nparticular, use `run_galaxy_tool_and_wait` for ordinary tools and\n`run_galaxy_udt_and_wait` to create and run a UDT. Do not replace these\nsupported operations with BioBlend tool creation, submission, status queries,\nor polling. Use BioBlend only when no available Galaxy MCP tool covers the\noperation.\n\nFor ordinary tools and UDTs, make one blocking execution call with an appropriate\ntotal timeout, normally 5400 seconds. Validation, submission, and terminal job\nfailures return directly; `new` or `queued` is not a failure. Do not query the\nsame job or submit a duplicate while that call is active. Replace a nonterminal\njob only when a concrete queue, destination, or route problem justifies it, and\ncancel the old job before submitting the replacement.\n\n### Output\n\nWrite `codex_output/answer.txt` only after the requested quantity has been\ncomputed successfully. The file must contain exactly one canonical answer line:\n\n- Numbers: decimal or scientific notation without thousands separators.\n- Percentages: append `%` only when the question requests a percentage.\n- Strings, genes, chromosomes, directions, categories, and choices: use the\n  exact requested label.\n- Do not include prose, Markdown, alternatives, citations, units labels, or\n  caveats.\n\nDo not read files outside the workspace except installed ski